    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0484" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1981-88v24/pg445"/>

                <head>204. Note From Director of Central Intelligence Casey to the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Clark)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d204-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1982-05-17">May 17, 1982</date>
                    </dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Bill,</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I am sending you personally this copy of “Prospects for Morocco,” an Intelligence
                    Community production which focuses on King Hassan and his regime. Although
                    published the morning of Monday, 17 May, I wish to ensure it reaches you prior
                    to the King’s upcoming visit. I believe the study projects a particularly
                    balanced view of internal and regional issues at stake for us in Morocco.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">William J.
                                Casey</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d204-f2"
                    /></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d204-a1.xml" xpointer="d204-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d204-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d204-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Reagan Library, Executive Secretariat, NSC Country File, Africa, Morocco (12/23/1981–11/19/1982). No
                    classification marking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d204-f2" n="2" xml:id="d204-f2-content">
                <p>Casey signed “Bill” above this typed
                    signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
